  "title": "Unified Title",
  "summary": "OmniDelta: Skill-Driven Budget Allocation for Token Compression in OmniLLMs and EvoSpec and Variational Speculative Decoding both focus on improving model performance through cost-efficient methods for evolving capabilities. The reports discuss cross-tier transfer strategies to optimize prompt selection and inference.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "The reports highlight the importance of attribute selection in vision-language models (VLMs) by avoiding class names and using image-based attributes to improve interpretable zero-shot classification.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "Both reports demonstrate how attribute prompts can be effectively selected by leveraging image data, addressing distribution shift issues.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The work on skill neologisms shows that soft tokens can be used to selectively acquire new skills without weight updates, improving capabilities on specific skills.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
  ],
